    {
      "node_id": "kg_doc_7",
      "node_type": "kg",
      "content": "Slavs are customarily divided along geographical lines into three major subgroups: West Slavs, East Slavs, and South Slavs, each with a different and a diverse background based on unique history, religion and culture of particular Slavic groups within them. Apart from prehistorical archaeological cultures, the subgroups have had notable cultural contact with non-Slavic Bronze- and Iron Age civilisations.",
      "depth": 0,
      "parent_id": null,
      "value": 0.9999999801379529,
